!Sample_title = Torpor+radiation 3
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM6022193
!Sample_status = Public on Jan 25 2023
!Sample_submission_date = Apr 05 2022
!Sample_last_update_date = Jan 25 2023
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Liver
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Danio rerio
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 7955
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = radiation (cgy): 32.64
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = temperature (c): 18.5
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = melatonin (um): 24
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = A melatonin group (28.5- melatonin) received melatonin daily for 10 days at a concentration of 24 µM for 10 days to reduce locomotion and arousal. A reduced temperature group (18.5-Ctrl) received a reduction in ambient temperature by 10°C from 28.5°C to 18.5°C to reduce their metabolism. An induced torpor group (18.5-mel) was established with a 10°C reduction in ambient temperature and the addition of 24 µM melatonin. A radiation group was exposed to a total whole body dose of 32.68 cGy.A torpor+radiation group was also established using a cold acclimatised group with melatonin that was also subject to the radiation protocol.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Total mRNA was extracted from liver tissue of the zebrafish using Qiagen’s miRNeasy Mini kit (Qiagen, Hilden, Germany).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = To prepare mRNA-Seq libraries the TruSeq RNA Sample Prep Kit (Illumina, San Diego, CA, USA) was utilized; 100ng of total input Liver RNA was used in accordance with the manufacturer’s protocol.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = High through-put RNA sequencing (RNAseq) was performed at the Queens University Belfast, Genomics Core Technology Unit on an Illumina Next SEQ 500 instruments with the mRNA library sequenced to a minimum depth of 50 million reads.
!Sample_data_processing = Sequence quality was assessed with FastQC to identify over-represented sequences and low quality reads
!Sample_data_processing = Low quality reads and over-represented sequences were removed with Cutadapt
!Sample_data_processing = The STAR aligner was utilised to align the RNA-Seq reads to the zebrafish genome (GRCz11)
!Sample_data_processing = HTSeq was used to determine the number of reads per transcript
!Sample_data_processing = DESeq2 was used for determination of differentially expressed genes
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: zebrafish genome (GRCz11)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: TXT file
